From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: divide by all of the elapsed time in retire_submit()

retire_submit() works out each submit's GPU clock as cycles * 1000 /
elapsed, with do_div(). do_div() takes a 32-bit divisor, so it divides by
the low half of the 64-bit elapsed time, and the if (elapsed) guard does
not stop a division by zero when that half is zero. On a3xx, which never
writes the per-submit stats, the slot used to hold stale memory and this
oopsed as "Division by zero"; 0106 made the slot read zeroes, but the
division itself was still wrong for any elapsed time of 2^32 ns or more.

Use div64_u64().

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c	2026-04-01 20:06:17.000000000 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c	2026-10-15 10:22:54.746683716 +0400
@@ -672,7 +672,8 @@
 	/* Calculate the clock frequency from the number of CP cycles */
 	if (elapsed) {
 		clock = cycles * 1000;
-		do_div(clock, elapsed);
+		/* do_div() would take only the low 32 bits of elapsed */
+		clock = div64_u64(clock, elapsed);
 	}
 
 	submit->queue->ctx->elapsed_ns += elapsed;
